<p> The first apportionment method we'll study is due to none other than Alexander Hamilton! </p>

<definition><title>Hamilton's Method</title>
<p>
    Start by giving each state its lower quota. Then, in order of largest fractional part, distribute the remaining seats.
</p>
</definition>

<exercise><title>The winners are...</title>
